	(text_box "Unlike the other video registers, the Chameleon's palette registers are memory mapped. \n\nPalette register 0 is mapped at F3400-F35FFh and palette register 1 is mapped at F3600-F37FFh. Only the lower two bits are significant, so each register repeats 128 times throughout their address space. This has some interesting implications; perhaps efficient use of string instructions to set the palette.\n\nFrom the CPU perspective, these registers are write-only. The video unit addresses them wtih C0 and C1 from the graphics serializers - in essence, they replace the CGA's traditional color MUX."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 43.18 26.67 0)
		(size 64.77 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
